      "explanation": "Tamoxifen itself is a prodrug, having relatively little affinity for its target protein, the estrogen receptor.  It is metabolized in the liver by the cytochrome P450 isoform CYP2D6 and CYP3A4 into active metabolites more affinity with the estrogen receptor than tamoxifen itself. These active metabolites compete with estrogen in the body for binding to the estrogen receptor. In breast tissue, 4-OH tamoxifen acts as an",
